1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:45,000
FlowPilot: a traceable investigation of simulated flux-spray defects.
Illustrative guidance; no equipment control or maintenance authorization.

2
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Measure the symptom. Preserve original machine records and units.
Image pixels do not establish weight, pressure or root cause.

3
00:01:40,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Adaptive questions retain uncertainty.
Unknown answers contribute no diagnostic weight.

4
00:02:30,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Five cause families, evidence-linked heuristic points and known gaps.
Reasoning mode is explicitly labelled: live or cached.

5
00:03:35,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Illustrative nozzle-only inspection, synchronized 3D, 2D and text.
An observation requires explicit confirmation.

6
00:04:35,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Record action separately from recovery. Calibration alone is insufficient.
Failed checks block resolution; retries require fresh confirmation.

7
00:05:45,000 --> 00:06:30,000
Review the saved result, evidence and timeline.
Restart creates a fresh case and preserves previous investigations.

8
00:06:30,000 --> 00:07:20,000
A clear nozzle does not exclude upstream restriction.
Reassess the evidence and keep the case open.

9
00:07:20,000 --> 00:08:00,000
Labelled fallback keeps the simulated demo usable.
Joint contract acceptance and revised expert approval remain pending.
